  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Locating Resources**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed only the `.gitignore` file exists initially. However, I remembered the user prompt and spotted a potential hotlinked image URL within the provided thought data. It\'s a Googleusercontent link, so that\'s helpful. Now, I\'m thinking about how to connect this to the rest of the problem.\n\n\n**Generating Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focused on visualizing the Turtle Rock Science Club\'s assets. I\'m exploring options, starting with generating images via the `image-generation` tool. This approach seems promising for creating custom illustrations or logos. I\'m also considering styled SVGs and standard icons for their flexibility and visual appeal. I believe `image-generation` provides the most powerful options to fit our needs.\n\n\n**Structuring the Homepage**\n\nOkay, I\'m now structuring the homepage according to the user\'s details. I\'m focusing on the Landing Page layout first. I\'m planning out a header, hero banner, join CTA, and latest lab logs. I\'m aiming for concise, informative content with clear calls to action. I want it to be visually appealing, and am now thinking about how the imagery of a styled Turtle Rock Science Club banner can interact with the different sections.\n\n\n**Defining Page Structure**\n\nI\'m now structuring \"About Us\" and \"Our Gallery\" pages. I\'m focusing on their key elements and content. I will start with an \"About\" teaser: \"Where Curiosity Meets Methodology\" with a picture and safety first badge, and a quote by Dr. Elena Vance. Then the page will have \"Nurturing the Next Generation of Naturalists.\" with images, missions, and interactive elements. \"Our Gallery\" will feature filters and a photo grid.\n\n\n**Expanding the Lab**\n\nI\'m now outlining key interactive components for the Experiments Lab. I\'ve got concepts for a user photo submission tool, a publicity and news page with announcements and events, and an interactive virtual lab. I\'m focusing on user engagement, so I\'m thinking how to integrate a lava lamp and chemical reaction simulator. I\'m considering their visual appeal and educational value.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the interactive elements for the \"Experiments Lab,\" building on the previous notes. I\'m prioritizing user engagement with an applet for the Turtle Rock Science Club that reflects the real-world activities. I\'m envisioning a \"Constellation Star Finder\" and a chemical reaction simulator with visual feedback, creating a functional science club app.\n\n\n**Creating Theme Options**\n\nI\'ve hit upon a great solution to support the provided visual variations! I\'m now designing an interactive theme selector. This allows users to switch between \"Turtle Rock Science Club\" and \"Kinetic Lab\" views dynamically. Each theme has a distinct logo, color scheme, and call-to-action (\"Join This Mission\" vs \"Reserve Bench\"). This addresses the user\'s specific examples and offers a fantastic interactive element.\n\n\n**Refining Lab Simulators**\n\nI\'m now refining the \"Interactive Lab\" components, aiming for high engagement. I\'m focusing on \"Lava Lamp Social,\" \"Volcano/Chemical Blast,\" and \"Star Finder Telescope\" simulators. The \"Lava Lamp\" will offer color and size choices for bubble effects. The \"Volcano\" will allow ingredient selection and explosion triggering. I\'m working on the Star Finder to display a sky view based on location. I believe these additions add a lot of real-world engagement.\n\n\n**Outlining Pages**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Field Trips\" and \"Lab Meetings\" pages, along with a submission form. Then, I am structuring the \"About Us\" and \"FAQ\" sections, including our founding story and core values. I\'m also planning the user scientist dashboard with avatar, level, reservations, and earned badges, which will be unlocked through simulator interaction. I\'ve now begun to organize these in a modular file structure, following instructions to avoid token limits.\n\n\n**Defining File Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the file structure for the project based on modular components. I\'ve broken down each part into its own file: `types.ts` for all shared types, `/src/data.ts` for static data, and individual files for each interactive component like `ThemeSelector.tsx`, `HeroSection.tsx`, `VirtualLab.tsx`, and more. I\'m carefully organizing these in a modular structure to maintain a clear file organization that will keep the site easy to manage.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 892645159
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
