        }
        lines {
          text: "              In the spring of 2018, three parents living in Turtle Rock Valley gathered in a backyard around a cardboard table to construct a basic solar filtration box. They wanted their children to witness the partial solar eclipse safely, but found that local schools lacked the specialized optics and dedicated lab time to explore the astronomical phenomenon in depth."
