  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing App\'s Role**\n\nI\'ve successfully created the JoinModal! I\'m now focused on understanding the responsibilities of `/src/App.tsx`. Currently, I\'m thinking about its role in managing global state, specifically the `identity` of the club, which can be either \'turtlerock\' or \'kinetic\', defaulting to \'turtlerock\'.\n\n\n**Defining App\'s Global State**\n\nI\'m now refining the global state managed by `/src/App.tsx`. I\'ve outlined the key state variables: `currentTab`, `userProfile`, `photos`, `missions`, `logs`, `announcements`, and `showJoinModal`. I plan to integrate `localStorage` for durable storage of `userProfile` and `photos`, ensuring data persists across sessions. The `missions` state will be dynamic based on the club\'s `identity`, read from `missionsData`. Finally, saving and reading from localstorage for the `userProfile`, photos, benches, and subscriptions will enhance durability.\n\n\n**Implementing Stateful Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the stateful logic within `/src/App.tsx`. I\'m focusing on managing `userProfile` updates: adding mission IDs to `reservedMissionIds`, incrementing `spotsReserved` and saving to `localStorage`. I\'m also incorporating the XP rewards system for actions like reservation, photo submission, newsletter subscription, and badge unlocking, triggering level-up notifications when appropriate and appending new badges.\n\n\n"
