    thinking: "**Refining Dashboard Layout**\n\nI\'m currently working to integrate the Bento Grid aesthetic into `src/components/Dashboard.tsx`. I\'ve started by examining the existing code structure. Specifically, I am focusing on modifying the outer row container, and then integrating the profile card and customization block elements. I\'m aiming for the relative z-10 font-sans. The next step will be to handle the className for `lg:flex lg:flex-row`.\n\n\n**Styling Profile Card Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on styling the individual components within the profile card. I\'m implementing the provided class names, paying close attention to the avatar circle, level and XP progression bar. I\'m applying the appropriate colors, fonts, and shadows to the progress bar track and handle, with the conditional color for the Turtle case. Finally, I\'m working on the form inline styling for name editing, which will be the last element to incorporate.\n\n\n**Implementing Button & Achievements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the achievements section and save button styling. I\'m focusing on the class names for the achievements grid boxes, distinguishing between active and inactive states. I\'m paying close attention to the visual cues and transitions, ensuring a clear distinction between the two, while also styling the save button to align with the overall design. Now, I will look at the achievement headers.\n\n\n**Styling Achievement Badges**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed styling for achievement badges. I\'m applying distinct color palettes for active badges, and using appropriate classes for both unlocked and inactive states. This includes styling the badge title, description, and \"UNLOCKED\" label. The next step is styling the Bench Reservations section, including the divider line and the header.\n\n\n**Designing Reservation Card Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the styles for the \"Bench Reservations\" section. I\'ve focused on the reserved missions cards, applying classes for container, title, date/time meta, and the release button. I\'m also styling the empty state reservations box, including title and subtitle elements with the correct typography and spacing.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `/src/components/Dashboard.tsx` to align the personal laboratory dashboard with the Bento Grid design theme. This replaces generic gray scales and card elements with glassy, high-contrast indicators, custom XP progress trackers, and detailed badge cards."
