    thinking: "**Visualizing Enhanced Design**\n\nI\'m exploring enhancing the visual representation of \"Turtle Rock.\" My current thinking centers on replacing the existing emoji `\360\237\220\242` with a custom SVG Turtle Rock logo. This would dramatically improve the visual quality and branding consistency, reflecting a more premium aesthetic by perfectly matching the official logo. It\'s about a seamless integration for a much better look.\n\n\n**Constructing The SVG Logo**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component\'s structure at `/src/components/TurtleRockLogo.tsx`, focusing on a clean SVG design. My current plan is to break down the logo into its constituent parts: an outer curved shape, uppercase \"TURTLE ROCK\" text along a path, and a central atomic symbol with glowing spheres. I\'m exploring the use of `<textPath>` for curved text, expecting native SVG support to work seamlessly. I\'m meticulously designing each element, planning the beaker shell, teal turtle, and \"science club\" text paths.\n\n\n**Simulating Text Positioning**\n\nI\'m now simulating coordinates for the SVG. I\'ve set a `viewBox` of `0 0 240 240` with a center at (120, 120). I\'m visualizing the placement of the atomic ellipses, considering radii of 25x75 or 30x85. I\'m focusing on text path placement: the top \"TURTLE ROCK\" arc from (45,115) to (195,115), and the bottom \"science club\" arc from (45,125) to (195,125). I\'m testing the textPath placement.\n\n\n**Confirming SVG Text Direction**\n\nI\'m now completely clear on how to orient the SVG text along the curved path. My main concern was ensuring the bottom text reads correctly. I realized if the path curves downwards from right to left, the text will be upright, solving any orientation issues. The initial \"right to left\" path configuration with sweep-flag set to 0, which means the text curves down (concave from the top), will allow the text to go upwards as needed. I\'ve validated this method now.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a highly precise, high-fidelity SVG React component for the **Turtle Rock Science Club Logo**. This component implements the custom sticker logo: the teal-colored turtle with a bubbling green beaker dome shell, surrounded by atomic orbital loops with glowing green node particles, and the playful blocky \"TURTLE ROCK\" and \"science club\" curved text paths. Using SVG ensures it is scalable, crisp, and performant."
