**Determining Secure Storage**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the best approach for securely storing account details on the backend. My current thinking is that Firebase, specifically its Authentication and Firestore services, offer the best solution. The system already considers Firebase as a durable cloud persistence solution, which is ideal for user data. I\'m exploring Firebase\'s security features to ensure user data remains safe and accessible.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Firebase Implementation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on Firebase. Specifically, Firebase Authentication is the perfect home for identity and authentication details, like emails and passwords. Simultaneously, Firestore (Cloud Firestore) will house richer account information, including roles, mission progress, and club configurations. The overall aim is to leverage Firebase\'s durability, scalability, and real-time capabilities. The setup tool will manage Firebase configuration for now.\n\n\n"
